=== KILL of a thread that is not there → ER_NO_SUCH_THREAD (1094), three spellings ===
KILL 123;
ERROR 1094: Unknown thread id: 123
KILL QUERY 456;
ERROR 1094: Unknown thread id: 456
KILL CONNECTION 789;
ERROR 1094: Unknown thread id: 789
=== BACKUP / RESTORE / PURGE — shape (d) "Expected: an SQL statement" ===
BACKUP DATABASE test TO 'foo';
ERROR 1064: SQL parse error: sql parser error: Expected: an SQL statement, found: BACKUP at Line: 1, Column: 1
RESTORE FROM 'foo';
ERROR 1064: SQL parse error: sql parser error: Expected: an SQL statement, found: RESTORE at Line: 1, Column: 1
PURGE BINARY LOGS BEFORE '2026-01-01';
ERROR 1064: SQL parse error: sql parser error: Expected: an SQL statement, found: PURGE at Line: 1, Column: 1
PURGE BINARY LOGS TO 'log';
ERROR 1064: SQL parse error: sql parser error: Expected: an SQL statement, found: PURGE at Line: 1, Column: 1
